1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:11,000
Toss a fair coin ten times, and you might get six heads. Small samples wobble. An A/B test checks if a change really worked, or was luck.

2
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:19,125
Split visitors at random. Half see the old page, half the new one. Then compare conversion rates.

3
00:00:20,830 --> 00:00:29,805
Significant is not the same as important. A tiny lift can be significant with huge traffic, but not worth the cost.

4
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:36,150
And not significant does not mean no effect. Maybe the test was too small.

5
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:41,360
Check guardrail numbers too, like complaints and refunds.

6
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:49,885
A z score beyond about two means a difference that big would rarely happen by luck alone.

7
00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:57,990
Decide the sample size first, run whole weeks, and do not stop early because you like the result.

